  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Space Exploration Technologies has $1.9B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date across 63 awards, with an average award size of $29.6M. Obligations are down 37.9% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $1.9B in the current fiscal year to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $6.4M and the Department of State obligated $3.1M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the largest NAICS market with $1.5B, followed by Satellite Telecommunications at $280M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $100M. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing shows $0. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity, while award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations. This snapshot highlights where federal dollars are concentrated and how activity compares to prior fiscal years.",
